      "id": "claim_f7d2220e4ad04848b8e5827414990f32",
      "statement": "The SHOPPERS permission pattern uses a single ACL permission with both $unauthenticated and user roles, not two separate permissions, because the ACL authorizer matches only the first permission it finds and two rules for the same path would make which one applies depend on role order.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.ts#L53-L65",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9d60a6b817811892714abd7ad9dd9576fbf8aaf9808d3aa0b7ff9e7cdc8a3bf0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7e2ffa2095cb4286aff08338aea4c6e7",
      "statement": "The catalog readFilter uses a $or query with two conditions: {purchasable: true} for flat products and {variants: { $elemMatch: {purchasable: {$ne: false}}}} for variant products, ensuring both product types appear while hiding draft/unavailable items.",
      "evidence": [
